{
  "comment": "Garments the MakeHuman creator bodies wear (docs/design/clothes-draw.md \"MakeHuman bodies\"). tools/makehuman/mh_creator.py fits every garment to each base it lists, so the garment gets that base's slider morphs, and mh_export.py writes it as its own FBX; the MakeHumanArt commandlet imports it as SK_MHG_<Base>_<Garment>. An apparel def names the garments it can be drawn as in visual.cuts (one or more names joined by '+'; a pawn draws one cut, picked by the item). mhclo is an asset folder or .mhclo under {mh_user} (MakeHuman's user data: the free asset packs from https://static.makehumancommunity.org/assets/assetpacks/index.html are unzipped there, see packs). A garment can name a different mhclo per base (female and male versions). \"bases\" limits a garment to some bases (women's cuts on the female base only, men's on the male).",
